## Files changed

**Render** — `js/render/pipeline.js`, `materials.js`, `sprite.js`, `parallax.js`, new `minions.js`
**Game** — `js/main.js`, `js/game/level.js`, `enemy.js`, `player.js`, `boss/base.js`, `boss/ulburjo.js`, `js/core/config.js`, `js/core/assets.js`
**Tools** — `tools/build-atlas.py` (rewritten), new `tools/stage1.mjs`
**Output** — all five atlases + manifest, `docs/stage1-notes.md`

## The 7 acceptance checks

| # | Check | Result |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `menu.png` — Enter starts without clicking | pass (focus on `menu-new`, Enter → cutscene) |
| 2 | `l1-right.png` | pass — face and sword point **right**, cloak trails left |
| 3 | `l1-left.png` after holding A | pass — face points **left**, cloak trails right; x-moment 52.93 vs 52.50 confirms a real mirror |
| 4 | `l1-enemies.png` | pass — 4 procedural silhouettes, no boss sheet reused |
| 5 | `l1-boss` / `l2-start` / `l3-start` | pass — via new `?level=N` / `?boss=1` |
| 6 | Zero console errors | pass (0) |
| 7 | Read each screenshot myself | confirmed below |

Check 7, from my own reading: no grain or noise anywhere. Kael's cloak is teal and his armour silver — not brown. The statue is grey stone with dark red, not white outlines. The level painting is visible behind the playfield in all three levels (the emerald shrine, the purple reliquary, the burnt-orange wood). L2 shows the purple `#7a3fa0` body with toxic-green lips; L3 near-black with ember lips.

## Two things to flag

**`.bunny-done` already exists** — created and committed by the *previous* session (`1c8aa64`, 23:06), not by me. I was told not to create it and didn't. But it now wrongly signals the whole rebuild is finished after stage 1. I left it alone rather than deleting a tracked file I didn't create; say the word and I'll remove it.

**My commit swept in 6 files I didn't author** — `assets/cutscenes/01–06.png`, which were untracked on disk. `git add -A` picked them up. Harmless, but outside stage 1's scope.

## Could not fully do

The statue's walk/run frames still carry a sliver of the neighbouring figure. The source board draws those poses *overlapping* — the robes run into each other — so no border-based key can split them. I flood the section once and partition by nearest label centre, so the dominant figure is correct in all 12 frames, but a sliver remains. Hand-masking would be needed to clear it.

Also: the far backdrop is dimmer than the brief's 55% and the sky gradient was darkened hard, because at the specified values the painting's emerald pool was brighter than the near-black platforms the brief also asks for, and the playfield disappeared. Both deviations are written up in `docs/stage1-notes.md`.
