Stage 1b is complete and committed as `d9645b6`. 14/14 acceptance checks pass.

**The two real bugs, both in the previous attempt's diagnosis:**

1. **The far quad was centred on the camera, not the view.** With a 600px crop in a 480px viewport, it only covered the left half of the screen — the right half was raw sky. That is what the brief called "huge blurry blocks," and it was also dragging L2's mean hue to 237°. Centred on the view, the crop spans the viewport exactly once at every pan value (`x 0..600` → `x -120..480`). L2 went to 260°.

2. **The scene pass stored `UnsignedByte` while working in linear light.** Linear values cluster near zero, so 8 bits per channel destroyed the dark half of every colour: sRGB `(30,14,5)` landed on `(3,1,0)`, turning burnt orange into yellow-green. Changing the render target to `HalfFloatType` is a one-line edit outside `parallax.js`, but it is what makes the hue targets measurable at all. I included it in the commit with that rationale in the message.

Worth flagging: my earlier attempts were tuning brightness and adding a per-level vertical offset to chase the 4.2° hue gap. Both were compensating for bug #1, and I removed them once the coverage bug was fixed — the final code has no hue-specific fudge.

**Verified beyond the numbers:** all three screenshots read as their subjects (L1 forest with vines, L2 full gothic arch, L3 procedural orange + bare trees, no `3.jpg`). I also exercised the custom `assets/bg/manifest.json` path with temporary 16:9 and non-16:9 art to confirm the centre-crop and no-404 requirements, then restored the shipped manifest and deleted the 3.4MB of unused experiment PNGs. `.bunny-done` was not created.

One note: there is no `package.json`, lint, or test script in this project, so `node tools/stage1b.mjs` plus `node --check` is the full verification available. `.bunny-loop.log` is left modified and uncommitted as harness noise.
