Stage 1c (partial): smooth glow, L2 platforms, elder leak

Three of the four items in docs/stage1c.md. The painted backgrounds are NOT
included: the three assets/bg/lN.png files were deleted during stage 1b before
this brief was written, and they are not recoverable from git, trash or cache.
Item 1 needs those files re-supplied.

Item 2, blocky glow. makeGlowTexture was a 32x32 radial gradient sampled with
NearestFilter, so the halo showed its individual texels as a grid of squares
over a dark backdrop. Now 128x128 with a smooth multi-stop falloff and
LinearFilter -- the only non-NEAREST texture in the game, since silhouette
crispness is what makes enemies read at 480x270. Halos are also clamped to a
40px radius so no entity can grow an additive wash across the backdrop.

Item 3, L2 platforms. tile/platform went from a solid #7a3fa0 to #1a0f22,
matching the L1/L3 rule: near-black body, accent only on the 1-2px top lip.
The green lip (#9be34a) is unchanged. The bright slab outshone Kael and read as
a foreground object.

Item 4, elder in L2/L3. Not level data -- the elder is only in L1's entity
list. The teardown in _loadLevel cleared this.enemies before the loop that was
meant to detach the old meshes, so the loop iterated nothing and every enemy,
shard and the elder stayed in the scene for the rest of the run. The meshes are
now detached first, and projectiles and a live boss are cleaned up too.

Verified with a scene-graph probe: the elder's 40x49 sprite is present at
384,32 in L1 and absent in L2 and L3 (it was in all three before). Glow
textures report 128x128 / LinearFilter, halo sizes 36px and 20px. L2 tile reads
0x1a0f22. Zero console errors. Screenshots in .scratch/stage1c/.
