Committed as `e160f4f`. All 3 fixes done and verified.

**1. Portraits now use the cutscene paintings, in CSS only** — `background-image` + `background-size` + `background-position`, 96×96 frame, accent border kept, `image-rendering: auto`. No new files, and the runtime canvas work is gone (`_makePortraits` / `_portraitDataUrl` deleted along with two dead element refs).

I tuned the rectangles by simulating what a 96×96 box actually shows for a given size/position pair and looking at it, three iterations each. Worth flagging: my first attempt rendered **entirely black** because I had the offset sign backwards — `background-position: -96px` shows the region *starting at* +96, not before it. Final values:
- Kael — `04.png`, size 320, position `-96px -46px` (window x 30–60%, y 14–44%)
- Elder — `03.png`, size 560, position `-320px -205px` (window x 57–74%, y 37–54%)

The elder needed more zoom than the brief's estimate; at 417 his face was small and shoved to one side. Both now show a single centred face filling the frame.

**2. Panels over the level are opaque** — `.story-panel` was `.82`, so the level showed through. Now `1`, leaving the 400 ms crossfade as the only partial state. I verified this rather than trusting the CSS value: screenshotting the panel area with the panel shown and hidden gives a mean delta of 55.7/765 with only 5% identical pixels, so the level is genuinely not leaking. I also split the shared `opacity` declaration — the cutscene's `.panel-art` stays at `.5` deliberately (a full-screen panel wants to read as a composed frame, which isn't what the brief was about) and previously both selectors inherited one value.

**3. Single level title** — the toast read "Santuario de la Brasa — Santuario de la Brasa" because the level-number string and the zone name are the same string and `beginPlay` joined them. Now shows once: "Santuario de la Brasa" (ES) / "Shrine of Ember" (EN).

`tools/story.mjs` passes **10/10**; its portrait assertion was reading `src="data:..."`, so it now checks the resolved background image and the real frame size. Screenshots in `.scratch/stage2b/` (`es-`/`en-deal-portraits`, `es-`/`en-deal-panel-04`, `es-`/`en-l1-toast`) all read and confirmed by eye. `assets/` is byte-identical; the untracked `assets/cutscenes/.bunny-loop.log` is not mine and I left it.

One note: `docs/stage2c.md` is in the tree as a new brief — I haven't touched it, since you asked for stage 2b only.
